\name{cellucid_history_tour_start}
\alias{cellucid_history_tour_start}
\title{Start the guided tour}
\usage{
cellucid_history_tour_start(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{branch}, \code{returns_to} (The step shown again when the tour ends), \code{steps} (Steps the tour shows after the opening), \code{tracker}.
}
\description{
Play the State panel's guided tour of the branch shown, from the opening to the step shown: each step is shown in turn with its caption and notes (a camera step is flown to), for a talk or a class. It returns once the tour plays; the person pauses, steps or stops it, or history_tour_stop does.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.tour.start} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_tour_start(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
